# Rust
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace ships binaries and reproducibility
# of the validation numbers depends on a pinned dependency graph.

# Python (crates/tepsim-py)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.pyd
.venv/
/dist/
*.egg-info/

# wasm / browser app
/apps/studio/dist/

# mdBook
/book/book/

# `book/src/validation/` is generated by `cargo xtask validate` and `cargo xtask
# deltas`, and it is COMMITTED on purpose: the book has to build for someone who
# has no gfortran and has not run the suite. Each page carries the command and
# the commit that wrote it, so a stale one is visible rather than merely absent.

# coverage and profiling
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage/

# validation scratch output (the committed golden traces live in reference/)
/validation-out/

# editors and OS
.DS_Store
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# Claude Code transient session state. Project-level settings, if any are added
# later, should be tracked deliberately rather than swept in by a broad rule.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.local.json

# The golden trace is committed on purpose: it is the fidelity preflight's
# anchor and must work without a Fortran toolchain. Not ignored.

# Assembled locally to rehearse what `.github/workflows/pages.yml` publishes.
/_site/
